sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-22> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Whether a set of upper/lower block pairs can be concatenated to give identical strings (the Post Correspondence Problem) is straightforward for two pairs, but already with three pairs there is computational irreducibility, making the question undecidable in general.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Post Correspondence Problem with three pairs is likely undecidable";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 12, “The Principle of Computational Equivalence”; section “Undecidability and Intractability” (from p. 753), p. 756. Scope: Post Correspondence Problem instances with small numbers of pairs"
}
